>with finite precision.  It seems that by investigating things down to
>the quantum level, we have in fact exceeded the precision of the alien
>machine, and are reduced to probabilistic methods.

No.  First, quantum mechanics is no more easily modeled by a finite
celluar autonoma than non-QM physics.  And it does not obviously
limit more the computational power of our universe.  Second, as long
as the idea that the universe really is following QM is consistent
with what we see, it can't be excluded in preference to the hypothesis
that we're all being simulated.

