Well, I just returned from my first California gun show after moving here
from the Bluegrass State of Kentucky.  I don't know that I'll be bothering
to attend any more of these.

The show today was sponsored by "Code of the West Productions" and was held
in Napa, California at the Town and Country Convention Centerrived
bright and early to find that parking was free.  This was a good start.
Then I found that admission was to be $6.00.  Yup six dollars.  Okay, this
must be one heck of a show I tell myself.  I stumble into the "convention
center", it has the floorspace of a basketball court, and what is the first 
thing I see?  Some guy selling stuffed troll toys for kids.  Oh look!  There
is someone selling cheapo sunglasses.  And over there!  Costume jewelry and
Mickey Mouse watches.

I must have come into the wrong door.  I'm in the flea market area, right?
WRONG!  I finally find some gun dealers, and begin to look around.  I bumped
into this big sign that said "NO ASSAULT RIFLES ALLOWED".  Oh yea, I'm in
California now.  There were a few guys standing around in Civil War costume
and sporting guns of the times.  A few german mausers.  Used this and used
that.  Not much in the way of new anything.  Of course the dealers all offered
to order for me.  That was nice of 'em, eh?

One thing's fer sure... "This aint Kansas toto!"

The last gun show I attended was in Louisville, KY.  I'm unable to recall the
sponsor, but this guy did shows all over the southeast portion of the U.S.
There were gun reps from the factory in attendance.  Ruger, S&W, Glock just
to name a few.  There were individuals who had EXTENSIVE collections of
pistols, muzzle loaders, rifles, shotguns and MACHINE GUNS.  Yup, you can\
still own a machine gun in Kentucky.  There was an MIA-POW contingent on hand
as well as other Viet Nam type groups.  Local gun clubs had set up tables to
hand out literature and recruit new members.  And best of all, almost everyone
who was visiting the show was carrying his or her weapon of choice to trade,
talk about, or just plain show-off.  All this and more for $1.00 parking and
$2.00 at the door!  Size?  Uh, well...I couldn't see from one end to the other.

I really like California, but I guess I'll just have to get used to the fact
that all the anti-gun nuts have just about killed the enthusiasm of owning,
making, trading, shooting, cleaning, selling or even using your gun as a 
door stop.

Thanks, I just had to get that off my chest.


